feat(nav): Wave 2 - command palette, Navbar split, breadcrumbs, related-pages chips

Wave 2 of the site improvements plan. Ships four navigation
improvements globally without introducing any new dependencies.

Command palette (Cmd/Ctrl-K)
- New src/app/components/CommandPalette.tsx: hand-rolled palette with
  fuzzy scoring, keyboard-first (arrows / Enter / Esc), and indexed
  entries for every route (35), every tracked country (30), and 14
  top metrics.
- Also opens on "/" when no input has focus, and via a global
  `cursor:cmd-palette:open` CustomEvent (used by the Navbar hint).
- Mounted once in the root layout so it's globally available.
- New Search hint button in the Navbar (desktop, lg+) with a Ctrl-K
  kbd chip.

Navbar reorganisation
- Split the previous 15-item "Analysis" dropdown into two:
  * Ledgers: Defense, Climate, Trade, Migration, Debt, AI, Health,
    Energy, Labor, Resource Atlas.
  * Analysis: Monetary Policy, Forecasts, Simulator, Development,
    Inequality, Trade Network, Economic Gravity, Economic Cycles.

Breadcrumbs
- New Breadcrumbs component (src/app/components/Breadcrumbs.tsx)
  driven by usePathname(). For ledger routes it renders
  Home / Ledgers / <Ledger Name>; for everything else it falls back
  to path-derived titles.
- Wired into all 10 ledger pages (defense, climate, trade,
  migration, debt, ai, health, energy, labor, resources).

Related-pages chips
- New RelatedPages component + data/relatedPages.ts curated
  adjacency map. Each ledger gets 4 hand-picked follow-on links
  (e.g. Defense → Trade, AI, Energy, Debt).
- Wired into all 10 ledger pages just above the footer.

RouteTracker
- Also mounts a RouteTracker in the root layout. Records visited
  routes into `explore_progress_v1` in localStorage (SSR-safe,
  dedup'd, capped at 1000). Consumed by Wave 3's
  ExploreProgressBadge.
